  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="58a8-4e2b-1c35-58b2" name="Low Countries (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #96 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This army list covers the Communal armies of Flanders from 1312 to 1453, the later date marked by the slaughter of the last rebellion in Ghent. The Flemish communes caused a shock wave across Europe with their victory over the previously invincible French chivalry at the battle of Courtrai in 1312. The key to their success was the pike phalanx, used much earlier than in Switzerland. Fiercely independent, the cities never stopped rebelling against their French and later Burgundian masters during the 14th and 15th centuries. Their early victories were overshadowed by the crushing defeats they suffered later. Infantry: Communal Infantry

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Low Countries]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Mercenaries: Up to 25% Artillery: You may have up to one Artillery per every full 700pts of your army.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
